      "writtenOn": "2024-07-15T22:55:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIW, I don\u0027t like the notifyBrowseNodeChanged() function, but it basically exists for the GetFolderItems state, which can fetch nodes from any scope. I\u0027d prefer to always be explicit about what we\u0027re calling, but it would have a lot of repeat code in the GetFolderItems state. So, we\u0027re explicit when we can be, and general when we must be.\n\nIn this case, this is the mRootNode of the device, which is always VFS scope, so this is fine. (Technically, its not even an AVRCP concept, and isn\u0027t something sent over the browse channel. Its our own concept to represent a device level node and we\u0027re calling it a VFS scope. But, details!)",
